'''Costa Serena''' is a municipality in the [[Cumará (comarca)|Cumará comarca]], [[Estret Province]], [[Balboa]]. With a population of 136,237 in 2026, it is an affluent coastal exurb known for its gated communities, landscaped residential estates, and a private university. Situated on the Shendan coast in the western part of the comarca, Costa Serena is one of the wealthiest municipalities in Estret Province by per capita income, and its residential character is defined by low-density, high-value housing separated from the surrounding agricultural and semi-rural municipalities by tree-lined boulevards and private security perimeters.

== Geography ==

Costa Serena occupies a coastal strip along the Shendan coast in western Cumará. The terrain is generally flat near the coast, rising gently inland toward the foothills that separate the comarca from the interior. The municipality's coastline features sandy beaches and rocky headlands, and the residential development is set back from the shore behind landscaped buffer zones. Elevations range from sea level to approximately 80 metres in the eastern uplands.

=== Climate ===

Costa Serena has a {{w|tropical monsoon climate}} ({{w|Köppen climate classification|Köppen}} Am), with average daily highs of 30 to 32 °C and lows of 22 to 24 °C. The wet season extends from May to November, with the heaviest rainfall between June and August. Annual precipitation averages approximately 2,200 to 2,500 mm. The coastal position moderates temperatures slightly compared to the inland comarca.

== Demographics ==

Costa Serena's population of 136,237 is concentrated in gated communities and planned residential estates. The municipality has a higher proportion of [[White Balboan people|White Balboans]] and mixed Balboans than the comarca average, reflecting its status as a prestige residential area. The [[Fosian Balboan|Fosian]] community is small but present, primarily associated with university staff and professional households.

== Economy ==

Costa Serena's economy is based on residential services, education, and local retail. The municipality's private university is a significant employer and draws students from across the Sant Cristòfor metropolitan area. Commercial activity is concentrated along the main boulevards, with boutique retail, restaurants, and professional services catering to the affluent resident population. The municipality has no significant industrial or agricultural base.

== Transport ==

[[CristoCarril]] [[Line A (CristoCarril)|Line A]] serves Costa Serena via the [[Costa Serena (CristoCarril)|Costa Serena station]], providing a commuter rail connection northward to [[Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal|Sant Cristòfor Central]] and southward along the Coastal Line. The [[E68 expressway (Balboa)|E68 expressway]] connects Costa Serena eastward to the [[E5 expressway (Balboa)|E5 expressway]] corridor at [[Brises, Estret|Brises]], and local roads link the municipality to the neighbouring western Cumará communities.

